Do not delete this file.

GitHub Pages runs every site through Jekyll unless this file exists, and
Jekyll silently DELETES anything whose name starts with an underscore. All
the optimised photos live in assets/images/_optimized/, so without this file
98 of the site's 127 image URLs return 404 and the pages load with no photos
at all — locally everything looks fine, which makes it a confusing one.

The file only has to exist; its contents are ignored. It is written out
rather than left empty so nobody deletes it during a tidy-up.

The underscore on _optimized is deliberate: js/autoscan.js skips folders
starting with _ so it never mistakes generated copies for your photos.
Renaming the folder would fix Pages but break that, so keep both.
